# Trivy Vulnerability Ignore List
# Last updated: 2025-10-18
# Rationale: These CVEs have no fixed versions available in Debian 12 (Bookworm) repositories
# All ignored CVEs have been risk-assessed and determined to be low-risk for our use case

# ============================================================================
# LibTIFF Vulnerabilities (CRITICAL)
# ============================================================================
# Affects: Debian 12 tiff package
# Status: No fixed version available for Debian:12
# Risk Assessment: LOW - We don't process TIFF images in our application
# We're a budgeting app with no image processing functionality
CVE-2025-8534  # Use after free in get_histogram (tools/tiffmedian.c)
CVE-2025-7709  # LibTIFF up to 4.7.0 vulnerability
CVE-2025-8176  # Use after free in setrow (tools/thumbnail.c)

# ============================================================================
# libxslt Vulnerability (CRITICAL)
# ============================================================================
# Affects: Debian 12 libxslt package
# Status: No fixed version available for Debian:12
# Risk Assessment: LOW - We don't use XSLT transformations
# libxslt is a transitive dependency, not directly used by our application
CVE-2025-9900  # Memory corruption in ID attribute cleanup

# ============================================================================
# linux-pam Vulnerability (HIGH)
# ============================================================================
# Affects: Debian 12 linux-pam package (pam_namespace module)
# Status: No fixed version available for Debian:12
# Risk Assessment: MEDIUM - Containers run as non-root user
# We run containers with non-root users and don't use pam_namespace
# Attack requires local user access with specific symlink race conditions
CVE-2025-6020  # Privilege escalation via pam_namespace symlink attacks

# ============================================================================
# Review Policy
# ============================================================================
# This file should be reviewed and updated:
# - Monthly: Check if fixed versions are available
# - On new CVE discoveries: Assess risk and decide to add/remove
# - Before production releases: Verify all ignored CVEs are still justified
#
# To check for updates:
# docker pull debian:bookworm-slim && trivy image debian:bookworm-slim
# docker pull nginx:stable && trivy image nginx:stable
